{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "date": "2026-09-25",
  "scope": "Direct DM_MPATH_PROBE_PATHS kernel ABI experiments on isolated mappings in disposable QEMU guests. These are independent of the new Guard integration and are not host deployment or full storage-health tests.",
  "interface": {
    "name": "DM_MPATH_PROBE_PATHS",
    "ioctl_hex": "0xfd12",
    "architecture": "x86_64",
    "target_mode": "bio",
    "mapping": "probe-target multipath -> probe-backend linear/error -> disposable USB decoy.raw"
  },
  "commands": [
    "python3 lab/kernel_probe_test.py --build-dir lab/work/version-study/kernel7/guest --expect available",
    "python3 lab/kernel_probe_test.py --build-dir lab/work --expect unsupported"
  ],
  "current_runner_sha256": "e2847c42eab98da98fad935c9137619339f223e3c6c4970c6a7790c3f2bbe04f",
  "self_review": {
    "final_runs_match_current_runner": true,
    "final_runs_match_current_qemu_runner": true,
    "all_recorded_guest_action_hashes_verified": true,
    "normal_user_host_execution": true,
    "qemu_block_backends_are_per_run_regular_files": true,
    "guest_safety_guards": [
      "ram_rescue_lab=1 kernel argument",
      "RAMRescueLab DMI product",
      "KERNEL-PROBE-ONLY USB serial and 32768-sector fixture size"
    ],
    "assessment": "No correctness issue requiring a runner change was found in final self-review. Failure history below records the fixed fixture mode/readiness issues and the corrected legacy errno expectation."
  },
  "interpretation": [
    "A zero return can occur without any probe read when current_pg has not yet been selected. Guard must not treat zero as proof of a completed read or comprehensive recovery.",
    "After a normal I/O selects current_pg, the healthy ioctl caused an additional lower-device read. An injected lower read error made the active path failed and returned ENOTCONN when no valid paths remained.",
    "The ioctl remained blocked while the lower mapping was suspended; a separate RAM shell continued to work. Releasing that mapping allowed the original invocation to finish. This does not demonstrate a hard deadline or cancellation mechanism.",
    "Repairing the lower backend did not make this ioctl reinstate a failed path.",
    "The tested 6.8 kernel returned EINVAL, including on a plain virtual USB block device. Do not infer lack of feature support from EINVAL alone; target capability/version checks and preservation of unexpected errors are required."
  ],
